                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "19836510",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197988663774",
                            "num_reviews": 415,
                            "playtime_forever": 22,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 22,
                            "last_played": 1450756277
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I... don't really know what to say about Heavy Metal Death Pirate. Some parts of it, like the story and art, seem as though they had a lot of effort put into them, if perhaps not that much skill. Likewise, it seems as though the developer may have dealt with some downright shadiness when it came to how Desura/IndieRoyale treated him. (as seen on his blog: http://singestudio.blogspot.fr/2015/08/final-comments.html )\n\nOn the other hand, the result is just a pile of crap that feels in many places as though the author had never played a side-scrolling shooter before, with wonky and giant hitboxes, a forced position in the middle of the screen that doesn't give you much time to react to enemies once you see them, enemies that are obscured by the distracting backgrounds, background objects that position themselves in front of enemies, controls that are never really explained, and long missions that you have to restart from the beginning if you die. The first \"side story\" is supposed to be a tutorial, but there doesn't seem to be any way to complete it or even get beyond the first screen, as the tutorial guy never continues talking after his first line.\n\nSo yeah. I hope the author doesn't swear off game development for good, but this was a terrible first effort in a lot of ways, and I wouldn't recommend it to anyone except people who are more patient with bad games than I am (and that's saying a lot...) and really want to play a game about the adventures of power-suited superheroes.\n\n(I did not complete this - I spent about ten minutes fighting with the controls and the apparently broken tutorial, and then after several tries completed the first real level. I tried the second level once, but decided there was absolutely no way I was going to enjoy this and that I would just delete it and be done with it.)",
